<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<CatalogFile xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" RequiredVersion="7.00" xmlns="urn:Microsoft.PlatformBuilder/Catalog">
  <FileInformation Id="FileInformation:Boling Consulting Inc.:raspi2">
    <Title>raspi2</Title>
    <Description>raspi2 BSP Catalog Items</Description>
    <Vendor>Boling Consulting Inc.</Vendor>
    <OSVersion>7.00</OSVersion>
    <FileVersion>0.1</FileVersion>
  </FileInformation>
  <Bsp Id="Bsp:Boling Consulting Inc.:raspi2:ARMV6">
    <Title>raspi2: ARMV6</Title>
    <Description>Raspberry Pi BSP based on BSP Template</Description>
    <PlatformDirectory>raspi2</PlatformDirectory>
    <CpuId>Cpu:ARMV6</CpuId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:IdleMon:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:PowerOff:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:SdRoot:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:SdOffload:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:Audio:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:AudioTest:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:VolTray:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:UsbHost:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:Ethernet:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:SdHost:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:VidDebug:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:Vc4Disp:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:RaspiDisplay:raspi2</BspItemId>
    <BspItemId>Item:CEonPi:GdiBench:raspi2</BspItemId>
  </Bsp>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:IdleMon:raspi2">
    <Title>CPU Idle Monitor (demo)</Title>
    <Description>Small window showing CPU load, idle percentage and GetIdleTime(), with a desktop shortcut. Sets BSP_IDLEMON=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_IDLEMON</Variable>
    <Location>Applications</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>CPU IDLE MONITOR SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\APPS\IDLEMON</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:PowerOff:raspi2">
    <Title>Shut Down dialog (poweroff.exe)</Title>
    <Description>Dialog with Restart, Power off and Cancel buttons, with a desktop shortcut. Sets BSP_POWEROFF=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_POWEROFF</Variable>
    <Location>Applications</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>SHUT DOWN DIALOG SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\APPS\POWEROFF</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:GdiBench:raspi2">
    <Title>GDI benchmark (gdibench.exe)</Title>
    <Description>Full-screen app with a desktop shortcut that times the display driver: solid fills, inverts, scrolling, text, uploads and screen readbacks, about 2 seconds each. Results are shown on screen and in the debug output (lines starting with "gdibench:"). Sets BSP_GDIBENCH=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_GDIBENCH</Variable>
    <Location>Applications</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>GDI BENCHMARK SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\APPS\GDIBENCH</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:SdRoot:raspi2">
    <Title>SD card as root file system</Title>
    <Description>Mounts the SD card (the FAT boot partition) as the root file system instead of \Storage Card. Its Windows folder is merged into \Windows over the ROM image, and files on the card persist across reboots. The SD drivers load in boot phase 1. Requires &quot;SD card host controller (Arasan eMMC)&quot;. Sysgen adds the SD Bus Driver, SD Memory, SD Standard Host Controller, FAT File System and Partition Driver components. Sets BSP_SDROOT=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_SDROOT</Variable>
    <Location>Storage</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>SD ROOT REGISTRY SETTINGS</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\FILES</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:SdOffload:raspi2">
    <Title>Load optional modules from the SD card</Title>
    <Description>Leaves the modules listed as "; SDOFFLOAD" in platform.bib (IE7 stack, network command-line tools) out of kernel.img and copies them to the Windows folder of the sdcard build folder, so they load from the SD card and take no RAM until used. Requires "SD card as root file system". Sysgen adds the SD Bus Driver, SD Memory, SD Standard Host Controller, FAT File System and Partition Driver components. Sets BSP_SDOFFLOAD=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_SDOFFLOAD</Variable>
    <Location>Storage</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>SD OFFLOAD LIST AND SCRIPTS</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\FILES</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:Audio:raspi2">
    <Title>Analog audio (Pi 1 3.5 mm jack)</Title>
    <Description>PWM audio driver (pwmaudio.dll) for the 3.5 mm jack of the Pi 1 Model B/B+/A+ (GPIO40/45 PWM fed by DMA). The Pi Zero has no jack. Sysgen adds the Waveform Audio component (SYSGEN_AUDIO). Sets BSP_AUDIO=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_AUDIO</Variable>
    <Location>Device Drivers\Audio</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>PWM AUDIO DRIVER SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\DRIVERS\PWMAUDIO</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:AudioTest:raspi2">
    <Title>Audio test (audiotest.exe)</Title>
    <Description>waveOut test app with a desktop shortcut: plays left/right test tones in several formats and reports timing and position; "audiotest file.wav" plays a file with PlaySound. Sysgen adds the Waveform Audio component (SYSGEN_AUDIO); needs an audio driver. Sets BSP_AUDIOTEST=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_AUDIOTEST</Variable>
    <Location>Applications</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>AUDIO TEST SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\APPS\AUDIOTEST</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:VolTray:raspi2">
    <Title>Volume tray icon (voltray.exe)</Title>
    <Description>Speaker icon in the taskbar notification area: click it for a volume slider and a Mute check box (right click: Exit). Started from the Startup folder; no desktop shortcut. Sysgen adds the Waveform Audio, Common Control and Standard Shell components; needs an audio driver. Sets BSP_VOLTRAY=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_VOLTRAY</Variable>
    <Location>Applications</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>VOLUME TRAY ICON SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\APPS\VOLTRAY</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:UsbHost:raspi2">
    <Title>USB host controller (DWC OTG)</Title>
    <Description>USB host controller driver (dwchci.dll) for the Synopsys DesignWare OTG core: low, full and high speed devices, hubs (split transactions), control, bulk and interrupt transfers. Needed for keyboards, mice, mass storage and USB Ethernet. Sysgen adds the USB Host Support and USB HID Keyboard and Mouse components; add other class drivers (e.g. USB Storage Class Driver) yourself. Sets BSP_USBHOST=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_USBHOST</Variable>
    <Location>Device Drivers\USB</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>USB HOST CONTROLLER DRIVER SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\DRIVERS\DWCHCI</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:Ethernet:raspi2">
    <Title>USB Ethernet (SMSC LAN95xx)</Title>
    <Description>USB Ethernet driver (smsc95xx.dll, USB client and NDIS miniport) for the SMSC LAN9512/LAN9514 built into the Pi 1 Model B/B+ (0424:ec00), with the MAC address from the firmware and DHCP. The Pi Zero has no Ethernet. Requires &quot;USB host controller (DWC OTG)&quot;. Sysgen adds the USB Host Support and Wired Local Area Network (NDIS, TCP/IP) components. Sets BSP_ETHERNET=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_ETHERNET</Variable>
    <Location>Device Drivers\Ethernet</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>USB ETHERNET DRIVER SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\DRIVERS\SMSC95XX</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:SdHost:raspi2">
    <Title>SD card host controller (Arasan eMMC)</Title>
    <Description>SD host controller driver (sdhcbcm.dll): BCM2835 PDD over the CE standard SD host MDD, PIO only. Mounts the FAT/exFAT partition of the boot SD card as \Storage Card (or as the root with &quot;SD card as root file system&quot;). Sysgen adds the SD Bus Driver, SD Memory, SD Standard Host Controller, FAT File System and Partition Driver components. Sets BSP_SDHOST=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_SDHOST</Variable>
    <Location>Device Drivers\SD</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>SD HOST CONTROLLER DRIVER SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\DRIVERS\SDHCBCM</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:VidDebug:raspi2">
    <Title>On-screen debug output</Title>
    <Description>Shows the kernel debug output on the display as a scrolling console under a small boot logo until the desktop starts. Already on in images with KITL; this item turns it on in images without KITL (IMGNOKITL=1, e.g. Release). Built into the OAL, so rebuild the BSP (not just make the image) after changing it. Sets BSP_USEVIDASDEBUGPORT=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_USEVIDASDEBUGPORT</Variable>
    <Location>Debugging</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>OAL DEBUG OUTPUT SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\OAL\OALLIB</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:Vc4Disp:raspi2">
    <Title>Display: VideoCore IV (vc4disp)</Title>
    <Description>Display driver (vc4disp.dll) for the BCM2835 VideoCore IV, the successor of the basic framebuffer driver. Currently the same as the basic driver: the desktop uses the framebuffer the firmware set up at boot (native resolution, 16 bpp). Choose one display driver; with none the image is headless (untested). Sets BSP_VC4DISP=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_VC4DISP</Variable>
    <ChooseOneGroup>true</ChooseOneGroup>
    <Location>Device Drivers\Display</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>VIDEOCORE IV DISPLAY DRIVER SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\DRIVERS\VC4DISP</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
  <Item Id="Item:CEonPi:RaspiDisplay:raspi2">
    <Title>Display: basic framebuffer (raspiBasic_ddi)</Title>
    <Description>The original display driver (raspibasic_ddi.dll, Microsoft flat sample): the desktop uses the framebuffer the firmware set up at boot. Kept as a known-good fallback for "Display: VideoCore IV (vc4disp)". Choose one display driver; with none the image is headless (untested). Sets BSP_RASPIDISPLAY=1.</Description>
    <Type>BspSpecific</Type>
    <Variable>BSP_RASPIDISPLAY</Variable>
    <ChooseOneGroup>true</ChooseOneGroup>
    <Location>Device Drivers\Display</Location>
    <SourceCode>
      <Title>BASIC DISPLAY DRIVER SOURCE CODE</Title>
      <Path>$(_WINCEROOT)\PLATFORM\RASPI2\SRC\DRIVERS\RASPIBASIC_DDI</Path>
    </SourceCode>
  </Item>
</CatalogFile>